cries out to the graves of her 25 year  old twin sons lang wang and thapuang she  pleads with them to come home for  christmas  the brothers from outing village in mon  district were in this pickup truck last  saturday when soldiers opened fire six  of the eight coal miners traveling with  them were shot dead  cognac led a search party when the  miners failed to return home after we  we came to know that the bodies are  there  some of my  friends those who came along with me  we started  they started  setting fire to three vehicles  and after that  i went down there and i was sitting  there  and then we all  they all started firing and i lay down  and stayed there  following the ambush another seven men  were killed when soldiers fired at  protesting villages another protester  was killed the following day  india's home minister said the soldiers  were acting on intelligence that rebels  were on the road adding that the  government regretted the incident  during the ambush a vehicle approached  the location and it was signaled to stop  however it tried to flee  following which the vehicle suspected of  carrying insurgents was fired upon  resulting in the killing of six out of  the eight traveling in it however it  turned out to be a case of mistaken  identity  but one of the two survivors told al  jazeera the truck driver was never asked  to stop by troops who fired from both  the front and back  son sean wang was the truck driver  they were ambushed they shot innocent  people who didn't know anything it  wasn't even at night or in the jungle it  was on the road in broad daylight  the killings have provoked protests  against the armed forces special powers  act which gives the military extended  powers in areas where rebels are  operating the afsbah law is enforced in  india-administered kashmir and large  parts of india's north-eastern states  soldiers have the power to shoot to kill  arrest without warrant or destroy  suspect buildings all with immunity from  prosecution as far must go and why  aspire is bad that is the recent example  14 innocent  indian  citizen indigenous people of nagaland  were killed by armed forces  we cannot accept we cannot tolerate  we are no second to citizen how does  government of india can kill the  innocent  civilian of the country  government leaders say the army needs  extra powers in regions where rebels  operate but as the week-long mourning  for the villages of outing goes on  nagaland and meghalaya state leaders are  appealing to their government ally the  bharatiya janta party to repeal the  contentious shoot to kill law  elizabeth paranam al jazeera new delhi
 

